        <briefdescription>
<para>Checks a condition and, if false, stops the test case. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The failure is reported and counted as for <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-expectations_1ga6db7427ada09e476aec67306ca5c0b74" kindref="member">expect()</ref></computeroutput>; then, when exceptions are enabled, the rest of the test case body is skipped, and the run continues with the next test case, as <computeroutput>ASSERT_*</computeroutput> in GoogleTest, <computeroutput>REQUIRE()</computeroutput> in Catch2 and doctest, and <computeroutput>BOOST_REQUIRE()</computeroutput> in Boost.Test do. Without exceptions, the test execution is aborted with <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner_1a7bc806540e65c21095ef1ea1ef970db2" kindref="member">runner::abort()</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para>The test case is stopped by throwing a private exception, at the end of the statement, after the optional message was appended. It is not derived from <computeroutput>std::exception</computeroutput>; a <computeroutput>catch (...)</computeroutput> in the test case body must rethrow it, and the body must not be <computeroutput>noexcept</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Expr_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the custom expression.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Constraints</title><para>Enabled only if <computeroutput>Expr_T</computeroutput> is a framework expression type or is contextually convertible to <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>, including by an <computeroutput>explicit operator bool</computeroutput> (enforced via a C++20 <computeroutput>requires</computeroutput> clause, with <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1checkable" kindref="compound">extension::checkable</ref></computeroutput>).</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>expr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Logical expression to evaluate. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sl</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional source location, defaulting to the current line. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>result</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The check result, a temporary created by the caller as the default argument, which the applications do not pass; it is destroyed at the end of the statement. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A reference to the check result, to which optional messages can be appended with <computeroutput>operator&lt;&lt;</computeroutput>; the check is reported when it is destroyed, at the end of the statement.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>The result must not be named, stored, or kept in any variable. A reference such as <computeroutput>auto&amp;&amp; r = t.expect (...)</computeroutput> compiles, but dangles after the statement; the message operator and <computeroutput>value()</computeroutput> can be called only on a temporary, so the named result cannot be used, and forcing it with <computeroutput>std::move()</computeroutput> is undefined. The check must be reported at the end of the statement, and not later. Write the message in the same statement, with <computeroutput>operator&lt;&lt;</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
Initialises the <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1check__result" kindref="compound">detail::check_result</ref></computeroutput> received as the last argument, a temporary created by the caller, with the kind <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a0726a1bc3b6f16245cb8a4b42fe0e70caba12fb48e2d23bb2bd2819f64d02ec7e" kindref="member">detail::check_kind::requirement</ref></computeroutput>, and returns a reference to it. The check result evaluates the condition when initialised, records a pass or fail when it is destroyed, and, if the condition is false, stops the test case by throwing <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1failed__requirement" kindref="compound">detail::failed_requirement</ref></computeroutput> (caught by <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case_1adb4333ecb107fee477156b661f0b1512" kindref="member">test_case::run()</ref></computeroutput>), or, without exceptions, aborts the test execution. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
